From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Mon, 02 Nov 2026 21:10:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: bound WMI endpoints by firmware PHY capability

QCN9274 hardware supports two radios, but board firmware may enable only
one PHY. Connecting the unused MAC1 WMI service then fails with -EPROTO.
The endpoint count also determines the HTC credit split.

The QMI PHY capability exchange completes before HTC initialization. Use
its valid radio count to cap the selected WMI endpoint count, retaining
the hardware-mode and device-tree limits and the existing fallback when
no usable capability is available.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/htc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/htc.c
@@ -779,6 +779,12 @@ int ath12k_htc_init(struct ath12k_base *
 		break;
 	}
 
+	/* PHY capability is queried before firmware startup. A chip's maximum
+	 * radio count can exceed the PHYs enabled by its board firmware.
+	 */
+	if (ab->qmi.num_radios && ab->qmi.num_radios <= ab->hw_params->max_radios)
+		htc->wmi_ep_count = min_t(u8, htc->wmi_ep_count, ab->qmi.num_radios);
+
 	if (!of_property_read_u32(ab->dev->of_node, "qcom,num-radios",
 				  &num_radios) && num_radios) {
 		num_radios = min_t(u32, num_radios, ab->hw_params->max_radios);
